// §13.4 — an array state is addressed one element at a time. There is no path
// naming the whole array: §7 has no aggregate value to assign to it, and the
// declared default already initialises every element uniformly.
//
// The index is checked at CONFIGURATION, not here: the extent is not known
// until §6.2b step 4, and this same file would be valid against one `n` and
// invalid against another.
x[1] = 2 (-);

k0 = 1 (1/s);
